  "description": "The WHEN OTHER arm at :129-133, which must be LAST (gate G30). DFHPF12 is a real AID that this program names nowhere, so it lands here rather than acting as one of the four keys that are named - the test is an exact byte comparison against each mnemonic, not a range. Control only arrives here after DFHENTER at :120, DFHPF3 at :122, DFHPF7 at :125 and DFHPF8 at :127 have each been tried and missed, in that source order. The arm sets WS-ERR-FLG at :130, places the cursor with MOVE -1 TO TRNIDINL at :131, and moves CCDA-MSG-INVALID-KEY, the fifty-character literal app/cpy/CSMSG01Y.cpy declares, into the eighty-byte WS-MESSAGE at :132, then sends once at :133 and falls through to the EXEC CICS RETURN at :138. No file is touched: no STARTBR is issued on this arm at all. The paging state is echoed back exactly as it arrived, which is what makes an unknown key harmless rather than destructive. The program LISTS transactions even though the class it becomes is named TransactionMenuController - the name is taken from the prompt and the behaviour from the source. Every value expected here was DERIVED STATICALLY, by reading app/cbl/COTRN00C.cbl against app/cpy/CVTRA05Y.cpy, app/cpy/COCOM01Y.cpy, app/cpy/CSMSG01Y.cpy, app/cpy/COTTL01Y.cpy and app/cpy-bms/COTRN00.CPY; it was never captured from a live COBOL run, because nothing in this environment can execute the program.",
